---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# hung_requests: the session list poll, a send and Stop when a request
# the web control room waits on is slow or never answers
# (go/tests/model/README.md). The failures other flows model (ui_sidebar,
# ui_thread, stop_interrupt) are reads that fail; this one is reads and
# sends that hang. Its twin, hung_transcript, is the thread's first
# transcript read and catch-up; the flow was split there because the two
# together were 7920 states and share no field.
#
# Every request goes through api.ts req(), a bare fetch with no timeout
# and no AbortSignal: a server that accepts the connection and never
# answers leaves the promise pending for as long as the tab lives. The
# contrast is palette.tsx getJSON and mention.tsx's skills read, which
# reject after 15 s and are shown as failures with Retry.
#
# List (app.tsx refresh): the poll (every 4 s, 12 s while a session is
# open) calls refresh(true), which returns at once while inFlight is set:
# one list read at a time. Every read sets inFlight and takes the next
# readSeq; only the newest read's answer lands and only its finally
# clears inFlight. A read that fails sets loadErr, which is what shows
# "Updates delayed · synced … ago · Retry"; a read that never answers
# sets nothing. A non-poll read (Retry, the refresh after a send or an
# action, leaving a thread) is not gated: it supersedes the hung one, and
# when IT answers, inFlight clears and polling resumes.
#
# Send and Stop (Thread deliver/stop, App deliverTo/act), on the open,
# loaded thread: a send is added to the Thread's `inflight` set as the
# promise deliverTo returns, and deliverTo does not return until its
# POST settles AND the list read in its finally (`await refresh()`)
# settles. Stop sets "Stopping", awaits Promise.allSettled(inflight), and
# only then POSTs /interrupt (then act's own `await refresh()`).
#
# Fields (Page role):
#   list      the newest list read: none | out | hung (a hung read never
#             answers; the page cannot tell it from a slow one)
#   skipped   a poll tick found inFlight set since the list last landed
#             (loadedAt is frozen and the poll did nothing)
#   delayed   loadErr is set: "Updates delayed … Retry" is on screen
#   send      the one send in flight, as Stop's inflight set sees it:
#             none | post (POST out) | posthung | read (its finally's
#             list read, which is the `list` slot) | readhung
#   running   the session's turn is running on the server
#   stop      Thread.stop(): none | waiting (awaiting inflight sends)
#
# Abstractions, each to keep the graph small:
# - one send at a time: the composer is `busy` while deliverTo is locked.
#   A send is a steer while the turn runs and a prompt otherwise; the
#   server takes either when the POST lands. A POST that hangs may or may
#   not have reached it; this model says not, which only moves `running`,
#   and no claim reads it.
# - Stop's POST /interrupt is one step with its effect: once the sends
#   settle it reaches serve and the turn stops (stop_interrupt models the
#   hold and SIGINT behind it). A hung /interrupt is not modelled.
# - TabHidden/Visible add no state: hidden only removes poll ticks, and
#   visibilitychange calls refresh(true), which is a PollTick. The mapped
#   TabHidden/Visible actions are PollTick.
# - the thread is open and loaded throughout; leaving it (a non-poll list
#   read) is the same step as RetryList for the list, and the transcript
#   side is hung_transcript's.
# - Answer/Fail/Hang are the server's choice per request. A request that
#   is out and not hung answers (fair) or fails; one that hung never does.
# - a superseded list read that is merely slow will answer, so a send
#   waiting on it is done when it is superseded; one superseded while
#   hung keeps the send waiting (its own promise never settles).
#
# Fairness: the page's own steps (the poll, the send's awaits, Stop
# proceeding) and answers to requests that are out are strongly fair.
# The person (Retry, Send, Stop), the turn (Finish) and the network
# (Hang, Fail) are not.
#
# Corrections to the mapped model, from the code:
# - "PollsSuppressed" is not permanent: any non-poll read (a send, an
#   action, leaving the thread; Retry is not on screen) supersedes the
#   hung read and clears inFlight when it answers. Polls stay suppressed
#   only while the person does none of those.
# - Stop does not await "deliverTo's list refresh" as such: it awaits the
#   send's own promise, which includes that send's own list read. A poll
#   that hangs does not gate Stop; the read a send made does.
# - The mapped TimedOut state does not exist: nothing in req() times out.
# - OpenSession, catch-up and the first read are hung_transcript's.
#
# The product does not meet the mapped invariants and liveness claims;
# they are left out so the check stays green, and each is spelled below
# with the counterexample fizz gave when it was added (the gaps are
# findings, not fixed here):
#
#   ListStaleShown  not (list == "hung" and skipped and not delayed)
#     PollTick, PollTick, ListHangs: the list read never answers, every
#     later poll returns early, and nothing says the list is stale.
#   StopNotGatedOnRead  not (stop == "waiting" and send in ("read", "readhung"))
#     Send, SendPostAnswers, Stop: Stop waits on the list read that the
#     send's finally started, not on anything Stop is about.
#   (liveness) StopReachesServe  always eventually stop != "waiting"
#     fizz's lasso ends with send == "readhung", stop == "waiting": the
#     send's POST landed, its finally's list read hung, and "Stopping"
#     stays forever with /interrupt never sent. Send, SendPostHangs, Stop
#     is the same.
#   (liveness) ListReRead  always eventually list != "hung"
#     PollTick, PollTick, ListFails, PollTick, PollTick, ListHangs, then
#     only PollTick: never re-read, though "Updates delayed" is still on
#     screen from the earlier failure and its Retry is the way out.

def supersede(list, send):
    # A non-poll refresh: a new newest read, not gated on inFlight. A send
    # waiting on a slow read is released by it (that read still answers);
    # one waiting on a hung read keeps waiting. Returns (list, send).
    if send == "read":
        send = "none"
    return ("out", send)

role Page:
    action Init:
        self.list = "none"
        self.skipped = False
        self.delayed = False
        self.send = "none"
        self.running = True
        self.stop = "none"

    # The interval (and a tab coming back): refresh(true).
    atomic fair<strong> action PollTick:
        if self.list == "none":
            self.list = "out"
        else:
            self.skipped = True

    atomic fair<strong> action ListAnswers:
        require self.list == "out"
        self.list = "none"
        self.skipped = False
        self.delayed = False
        if self.send == "read":
            self.send = "none"

    atomic action ListFails:
        require self.list == "out"
        self.list = "none"
        self.skipped = False
        self.delayed = True
        if self.send == "read":
            self.send = "none"

    atomic action ListHangs:
        require self.list == "out"
        self.list = "hung"
        if self.send == "read":
            self.send = "readhung"

    # The sidebar's Retry, only on screen with loadErr.
    atomic action RetryList:
        require self.delayed
        self.list, self.send = supersede(self.list, self.send)

    atomic action Send:
        require self.send == "none"
        self.send = "post"

    # Landed or failed, deliverTo's finally reads the list (not gated).
    atomic fair<strong> action SendPostAnswers:
        require self.send == "post"
        self.running = True
        self.send = "read"
        self.list = "out"

    atomic action SendPostFails:
        require self.send == "post"
        self.send = "read"
        self.list = "out"

    atomic action SendPostHangs:
        require self.send == "post"
        self.send = "posthung"

    # Stop (Esc, the button, the palette), guarded while stopping.
    atomic action Stop:
        require self.running and self.stop == "none"
        if self.send == "none":
            # POST /interrupt reaches serve; act then reads the list.
            self.running = False
            self.list, self.send = supersede(self.list, self.send)
        else:
            self.stop = "waiting"

    # allSettled resolved: POST /interrupt, then act's refresh.
    atomic fair<strong> action StopProceeds:
        require self.stop == "waiting" and self.send == "none"
        self.stop = "none"
        self.running = False
        self.list, self.send = supersede(self.list, self.send)

    atomic action Finish:
        require self.running
        self.running = False

action Init:
    page = Page()

# The poll never stacks a read on one still out: a tick that finds one
# out or hung only notes it was skipped.
always assertion SkippedOnlyWhileOut:
    return not page.skipped or page.list != "none"

# A send waiting on its list read is waiting on the newest one.
always assertion SendReadIsTheListRead:
    return page.send != "read" or page.list == "out"

# A request that is out and not hung is answered or reported.
always eventually assertion ListReadSettles:
    return page.list != "out"

# A send whose requests answer ends: only a hang keeps it in flight.
always eventually assertion SendSettlesUnlessHung:
    return page.send in ("none", "posthung", "readhung")

# A Stop with nothing hung reaches serve: the only way it waits forever
# is a send that hung (StopReachesServe above).
always eventually assertion StopProceedsUnlessHung:
    return page.stop != "waiting" or page.send in ("posthung", "readhung")
